      "writtenOn": "2022-03-03T20:30:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "A few issues here:\n- The reason we had two methods here was to avoid default arguments. I personally prefer default arguments, but let\u0027s stick with the status quo and the [style guide](https://engdoc.corp.google.com/eng/doc/devguide/cpp/styleguide.md?cl\u003dhead#Default_Arguments)\n- The parameters should be in the same order, regardless of which overload you use. (Here, the first one places `colorDepth` right after `bitsPerComponent`, but another one snuck in between them for the second overload.)\n- I think in most cases, the `colorDepth` should match the `bitsPerComponent`. (This is more or less what we\u0027ve presumed elsewhere.) But for most `SkCodec` subclasses, you\u0027ve left it set to `0`. You could fix this without changing the rest of the code with something like\n\n  static SkEncodedInfo Make(int width, int height, Color color, Alpha alpha,\n      int bitsPerComponent) {\n    return Make(width, height, color, alpha, bitsPerComponent, nullptr);\n  }\n  static SkEncodedInfo Make(int width, int height, Color color, Alpha alpha,\n      int bitsPerComponent, std::unique_ptr\u003cICCProfile\u003e profile) {\n    return Make(width, height, color, alpha, bitsPerComponent, profile,\n                bitsPerComponent);\n  }\n  static SkEncodedInfo Make(int width, int height, Color color, Alpha alpha,\n      int bitsPerComponent, std::unique_ptr\u003cICCProfile\u003e profile, int colorDepth) {\n      ...\n  }",
